      "summary": "Add gameStateTexture to texture manager (#1634)",
      "description": "* Introduce game state texture\n\nTo be able to have shader effects based on current game state\nCurrently only exposes failure meter and song lengt/position\n\n* Fix game state texture using wrong texture format\n\nR16 is unorm, not f16 - the raw f16 bit patterns were being\nnormalized on sampling, reading back garbage values\n\n* Add SongTimer shader\n\nNixie tube style MM:SS / MM:SS song clock for venue quads,\nrendered from the game state global texture.\n\nDigit SDFs based on https://www.shadertoy.com/view/4dc3zr\n\n* Add gamestate.hlsl accessor include for game state texture\n\nShaders access texels by index through stable named accessors,\nso extending the game state with new fields (always appended)\nkeeps existing shaders working unchanged\n\n* Extend game state texture with venue-reactive values\n\nAdds song progress, countdown, paused/practice/speed flags,\nbeat and measure phases, star power active/charge, crowd\nintensity, band accuracy, combo multiplier and stars.\n\nTexels are append-only; shaders read them through the stable\naccessors in gamestate.hlsl\n\n* Add beat pulse torus showcase shader\n\nVertex-displaced torus that spikes on each beat with an extra\nkick on the downbeat; tint follows the fail meter\n\n* Add beat spike sphere showcase shader\n\nSphere with per-vertex noise spikes gated by the beat pulse,\naccented on the downbeat\n\n* Add beat ripple plane showcase shader\n\nFloor plane with concentric vertex-displaced ripples emanating\non every beat, brighter wave on the downbeat\n\n* Add beat wave grid showcase shader\n\nRow of cubes bobbing as a traveling wave, one wave per beat;\nphase derives from world position so no per-object setup\n\n* Add star power crystal showcase shader\n\nFills with light as star power charges, ignites with a fresnel\nrim and energy scroll while active\n\n* Add heartbeat orb showcase shader\n\nDouble-thump pulse that races and reddens as the fail meter\ndrops; rate and amplitude scale with danger\n\n* Add crowd wave plane showcase shader\n\nBanner whose waves grow bigger, faster and choppier as crowd\nintensity rises\n\n* Add song progress arc showcase shader\n\nTorus arc filling with song progress; depletes as a countdown\nring during the pre-song delay\n\n* Add song timer to sample venue\n\nPlaces the nixie-style song clock on the stage alongside the\ngame state showcase objects"
